# Case D — Roster Export Automation

## Client and problem
- **Client:** Mr. Ring (teacher, Pomfret School); eventually all ~90 teachers.
- **Problem:** Canvas has no clean one-click roster export. Every midterm and finals, teachers copy rosters out of Canvas, paste-special into Sheets to strip links, move names into a Google Doc to write comments, then copy comments into Sundial (Blackbaud MySchoolApp), export a PDF, and email it.
- **Goal:** (1) pull the roster from Canvas automatically, (2) generate a clean Google Doc per class for writing comments, (3) Phase 2: push finished comments back into Sundial via the Blackbaud SKY API.

## Team
- Developers: James Lake, Magnus Songhurst. Club lead: Cayden Auyang. Former developer: Jay Youm (Graduated); do not list him as an active team member.

## Stack and architecture (decided — do not reopen)
- **Google Apps Script bound to a Google Sheet.** No server, no Python, no Chrome extension. Files are copied into the Apps Script editor; this repo is the source of truth.
- `Code.gs` menu ("Canvas Tools") and orchestration · `CanvasAPI.gs` Canvas REST wrapper (courses + rosters, paginated, personal bearer token per teacher) · `DocBuilder.gs` creates a Drive folder, one Doc per class, one tab per student (falls back to page breaks if Docs tabs fail) · `DocReader.gs` reads completed Docs back · `SundialAPI.gs` Blackbaud SKY API placeholder (Phase 2, stubbed with TODOs) · dialogs: `TokenDialog.html`, `CourseSelector.html`, `SundialSetup.html`, `ExportDialog.html` · `appsscript.json` manifest and OAuth scopes.
- Secrets live in `PropertiesService.getUserProperties()` (`SUNDIAL_SUBSCRIPTION_KEY`, `SUNDIAL_CLIENT_ID`, Canvas token) and are set through the dialogs. Never hardcode them.

## Constraints and gotchas
- Docs "tabs" API support is new; keep the page-break fallback in `DocBuilder.gs` working.
- Canvas uses `sortable_name` ("Last, First"); Sundial's format is TBD. Use `normalizeName_()` for matching.
- Phase 2 is **blocked** until school IT registers the app and grants SKY API OAuth access; no public docs confirm a write endpoint for progress-report comments. Keep `SundialAPI.gs` stubs clearly marked `TODO` rather than inventing endpoints.
- `appsscript.json` must stay valid JSON; add OAuth scopes there when new Google services are used.

## Status and next steps
- 🟢 Phase 1 built: Canvas → Google Docs generation. 🟡 Phase 2 blocked on SKY API access.
- Next: test Phase 1 with Mr. Ring's real Canvas account; follow up with IT on SKY API; confirm a comments write endpoint exists; survey other departments' comment formats; package as a shared template for all teachers.
